    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d132">

                <pb facs="0219" n="121" xml:id="pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002 Manchuria/125: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan (Grew) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-06-29T23:00:00+09:00">June 29, 1932—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 29—1:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>17. Following telegram received from the Consul at Dairen: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“June 29, 4 p.m. Ex-commissioner Fukumoto relinquished custody of Dairen customhouse to
                            British assistant. Former in new customhouse and depositing customs
                            charges under his name Yokohama Specie Bank. Chinese that elected to
                            work with new customhouse striking, disturbing traffic. In case goods
                            pass through Dairen without duties payment at new customhouse, duties
                            must be paid at Manchurian border or be detained.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
